-pwd
    Print the Pathname of the working directory

-ls
    List Content of directories

-ls -p
    List directory and put a slash (/) after each entry is a directory

-cd <Foldername>
    Change working directory to Foldername

-cd ..
    Change to the directory one level up

-cd
    Change to your home directory

-cd ../../..
    Change to the directory three levels up

-cd /
    Change to the top most level directory (root directory)

-mkdir <Foldername>
    Make a directory named Foldername

-mkdir <Foldername1 / Foldername2>
    Create a directory named Foldername2 undernearth the one named Foldername1

-rmdir <Foldername>
    Remove an empty directory called Foldername

-rm -r <Foldername>
    Removed the Foldername that is not empty

-mv <Old Foldername> <New Foldername>
    Rename the directory named from old to New